MerkleAdapterCutoff
├── Reports close allocation and withdrawal buckets at a scheduled cutoff
│   ├── Before-cutoff allocations become spendable in the next accepted report exactly once
│   ├── Allocations at or after cutoff stay reserved until the following report
│   └── Withdrawal requests before, at, and after cutoff mature in their corresponding reports
├── Only the open bucket permits matching and cancellation
│   ├── Before-cutoff withdrawals can be matched, reduced, or cancelled
│   ├── Before-cutoff pending allocations can be returned immediately
│   └── After-cutoff writes preserve the frozen bucket and only modify deferred balances
├── Reports must include the frozen bucket in their snapshot
│   ├── A snapshot before cutoff cannot be cached or accepted by the curator
│   ├── A snapshot exactly at cutoff is eligible
│   ├── Delayed reports preserve deferred writes and select a future cutoff
│   ├── Post-snapshot deposits, cancellation and reserve withdrawals preserve the closed batch
│   └── Rejected or frozen reports preserve cutoff, nonce, and queued funds
└── Withdrawal losses preserve reserves
    ├── Matured reserves and deferred allocations survive a loss in the frozen bucket
    └── Either submission window caps released withdrawals to surviving NAV
